# Pre-merge review (CodeRabbit and Codex CLI)

## No push until both tools are satisfied

**Do not `git push`** until **CodeRabbit** and **Codex CLI** are satisfied for the current diff. Local **`git commit`** during iteration is allowed. “Satisfied” = triage done, all **must-fix** items the author accepts are resolved, and optional or rejected items are explained on the PR where useful.

## Install when binaries are missing

If **`coderabbit`** or **`codex`** is not on `PATH`, **try installing** (use what the environment supports):

- **CodeRabbit CLI:** `curl -fsSL https://cli.coderabbit.ai/install.sh | sh` or `brew install coderabbit`; then `coderabbit auth login`. Docs: https://docs.coderabbit.ai/cli
- **Codex CLI:** `npm install -g @openai/codex` or `brew install --cask codex`; complete auth per `codex` prompts.

If install fails after a reasonable attempt, document commands + errors on the PR and **do not push** until both tools can run elsewhere.

## Triage feedback (not every comment needs a code change)

- **Implement** when it fixes correctness, security, API/spec mismatch, bugs, missing tests, or clear project-convention violations.
- **Decline or defer** low-value style-only or redundant-comment suggestions; add a short PR reply with rationale.

## Workflow

1. **CodeRabbit** — Ensure the PR gets CodeRabbit review; use the CLI per docs if applicable.
2. **Codex** — Run `codex` on the tree or diff per team practice.

Keep **`.coderabbit.yaml`** aligned when changing review behavior there (also update **AGENTS.md**, **CLAUDE.md**, **`docs/versioning.md`**, **`.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc`**, and this file).

See **AGENTS.md** for the canonical wording.
